Whoah....  This would make the elven race quite a bit overpowered,
especially given the increased enchantability of elven armour.  Starting
with gloves is somewhat of a stretch as well.  I'd much rather see the
race be either given a non-metallic version of a weapon, or given a
suitable wooden alternative.  The game currently has a good balance with
this, given that you sometimes can't find a pair of gloves until you run
into a guard/soldier type or wish for some gauntlets.

I do like the idea of mithril not hindering spellcasting, although I
think equating it with non-metal armour would be far too overpowering.
Perhaps reduced interference, and only on elven mithril.  Who's ever
heard of magical dwarfs?

Although I'd love to have an elvish wizard start with gloves and a nice
set of non-spell-hindering elvish-mithril, it would just be a wee over
the top.

